  body: "# Claim in the prescribed manner\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured claims guidance distinguishes
    a claim made through an accepted procedure from an intention to claim, and describes benefit-specific written,
    electronic and telephone routes.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThere is no universal rule that a claim requires
    paper or that every telephone contact is a claim. Particular benefits and routes have exceptions, and making
    a claim correctly does not prove entitlement.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 02048, PDF page 15](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68d934f23ff62c51c1a7a2/dmg-v-1-ch-2.pdf#page=15)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 2: Claims.\n- [DMG 02082, PDF page 26](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68d934f23ff62c51c1a7a2/dmg-v-1-ch-2.pdf#page=26)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 2: Claims.\n- [DMG 02084, PDF page 26](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a68d934f23ff62c51c1a7a2/dmg-v-1-ch-2.pdf#page=26)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 2: Claims.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of the 15 September
    2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance, not a consolidated
    statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an
    entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file positions. Machine
    extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve extracted text;
    no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability remain
    separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch2` PDF SHA-256: `218f6a34945a5dd17cdccb1737ea317b2dcfd1ab62f66a9a0b8d681202e8934f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `77cb8966f05e501c4d970026bdfcd5bc271abe17a546b02ec8c8704395e56ee3`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-intention-to-claim
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The paragraph distinguishes an intention expressed by telephone from a claim and expressly
      names benefit-specific telephone exceptions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch2/0026
      quote: "02084 An intention to claim stated in a phone conversation is not a claim in the prescribed manner
        1 (but\nsee DMG 02073, and 02131 for claims to SFFP, BB, RP, GRB, SAPs and SPC made by telephone). For AA\n\
        and DLA there are provisions which allow the date of claim to be backdated to the date of a request for
        a\nclaim form. This includes oral requests made, for example, using the Benefit Enquiry Line.\n\n\n    \
        \                                                                                                 1 R(F)
        1/92\n\n\n\nWritten communication - sufficient to constitute a claim for benefit"
      locator: DMG 02084
